21:    Extend each black marker into a full divider line through its colored rectangle.
22:
23:    Input structure
24:    - The grid is partitioned into non-square monochrome rectangular regions.
25:    - A unique rare marker color appears as isolated pixels inside those regions.
26:    - Each region is otherwise filled with exactly one non-marker color.
27:
28:    Rule
29:    - For each wide region, replace the full region-height column through every
30:      marker with the marker color.
31:    - For each tall region, replace the full region-width row through every
32:      marker with the marker color.
33:    - Preserve colored regions that contain no marker.
34:
35:    Key insight
36:    - The marker does not spread globally; the aspect ratio of its own rectangle
37:      chooses the perpendicular divider direction and the rectangle bounds stop it.
38:    """
39:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
